From 4e0dc0523bd98adbd45ce1c66dd1a96d4f6a3ec9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luiz Augusto von Dentz <luiz.von.dentz@intel.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 16:16:35 -0500
Subject: Bluetooth: mgmt: Reject zero multi advertising rotation duration
Git-commit: 4e0dc0523bd98adbd45ce1c66dd1a96d4f6a3ec9
Patch-mainline: v7.4-rc5
References: git-fixes

A zero def_multi_adv_rotation_duration makes
hci_schedule_adv_instance_sync() requeue itself with no delay, spinning
the request workqueue. Reject it in Set Default System Configuration.

Reported-by: Sashiko <sashiko-bot@kernel.org>
Link: https://sashiko.dev/#/bug/linux-24ecb695-0c5c-408a-a016-a980c3115e95
Fixes: 17896406ff35 ("Bluetooth: implement read/set default system parameters mgmt")
Assisted-by: OpenCode:claude-fable-5.2
Signed-off-by: Luiz Augusto von Dentz <luiz.von.dentz@intel.com>
Acked-by: Takashi Iwai <tiwai@suse.de>

---
 net/bluetooth/mgmt_config.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/net/bluetooth/mgmt_config.c b/net/bluetooth/mgmt_config.c
index 6a617656bfbe..834220072450 100644
--- a/net/bluetooth/mgmt_config.c
+++ b/net/bluetooth/mgmt_config.c
@@ -224,6 +224,14 @@ int set_def_system_config(struct sock *sk, struct hci_dev *hdev, void *data,
 				MGMT_STATUS_INVALID_PARAMS);
 		}
 
+		/* A zero rotation duration would make the advertising instance
+		 * scheduler requeue itself with no delay.
+		 */
+		if (type == 0x000c && !TLV_GET_LE16(buffer))
+			return mgmt_cmd_status(sk, hdev->id,
+				MGMT_OP_SET_DEF_SYSTEM_CONFIG,
+				MGMT_STATUS_INVALID_PARAMS);
+
 		buffer_left -= exp_len;
 		buffer += exp_len;
 	}
